libsanitizer: define the MIPS ABI constants when musl does not

sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h picks struct_kernel_stat_sz with
(_MIPS_SIM == _ABIN32) but includes nothing that defines _ABIN32. glibc ships a
top-level <sgidefs.h> that gets pulled in transitively; musl does not ship one
at all, and its asm/sgidefs.h does not define these either. The result on a
mipsel musl target is seventeen copies of

    error: '_ABIN32' was not declared in this scope

and, because struct_kernel_stat_sz is then not a constant expression, a
follow-on "non-constant condition for static assertion" in
sanitizer_platform_limits_linux.cpp.

_MIPS_SIM is predefined by the compiler on MIPS, so only the ABI constants are
missing. Their values are fixed by the o32/n32/n64 ABI numbering and are the
same ones glibc's <sgidefs.h> has always used.

Signed-off-by: OpenIPC AI team <ai@openipc.org>

--- a/libsanitizer/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h
+++ b/libsanitizer/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@
 #include "sanitizer_internal_defs.h"
 #include "sanitizer_platform.h"
 
+#if defined(__mips__) && !defined(_ABIN32)
+/* musl ships no top-level <sgidefs.h>; glibc does, and the code below assumes
+   it has been pulled in transitively. Values are the fixed o32/n32/n64 ABI
+   numbering. */
+# define _ABIO32 1
+# define _ABIN32 2
+# define _ABI64  3
+#endif
+
 #if SANITIZER_APPLE
 #include <sys/cdefs.h>
 #if !__DARWIN_ONLY_64_BIT_INO_T
